# Line endings are not stored in a commit - they are whatever the last tool to
# write the file happened to emit, and git cannot see the difference because
# both forms normalise to the same blob. That is how this tree ended up mixed.
#
# This pins it: text is still stored normalised (LF) in the repository, but any
# file git writes - clone, checkout, reset, merge - lands in the working tree as
# CRLF on every machine, whatever that clone's core.autocrlf happens to be.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.wav binary
*.zip binary
